B.a3P=new A.b6("AutoSense AI \u2022 v1.0.0+6\nPublisher: Youssef Ahmed\nSupport: youssefahmed4010@gmail.com\nPrivacy policy: https://autosense-api.vercel.app/privacy\nSubscription terms: https://autosense-api.vercel.app/terms\n\nYour choices\nThe demo and live scanner dashboard run on your device. Bluetooth discovery uses nearby device names and identifiers to connect to the scanner you select. On older Android versions, Bluetooth discovery requires a location permission; AutoSense does not request GPS coordinates. Wi-Fi mode connects to the adapter address you enter.\n\nDiagnostic requests & Hybrid Smart Mode\nWhen you request guidance, the app sends your selected vehicle, DTC codes, symptoms, safety selections, notes and input source over HTTPS to the configured diagnostic service, or processes them directly on-device via the offline diagnostic engine when offline. Code lookup sends the requested code. Do not enter names, contact details or other personal information in notes. The cloud backend processes requests in memory without a user database.\n\nStorage and sharing\nHistory and recorded runs are kept in app memory and disappear when the app process ends. Reports or CSV data you copy are placed on your device clipboard. This version has no accounts, ads, analytics or enabled cloud history.\n\nSubscriptions (Freemium & AutoSense Pro)\nBasic 56-code DTC lookup and the HP & torque calculator are free. AutoSense Pro (EGP 99/month or EGP 999/year with a 3-day free trial) is processed through Google Play. Purchase tokens are sent over HTTPS to the configured backend to verify subscription status and expiry. AutoSense does not collect card details.\n\nControls & boundaries\nYou can disconnect a scanner, cancel a run, revoke permissions in Android Settings, and close the app to end its session. Hardware compatibility is experimental. Guidance lists possibilities, not definite diagnoses. Run estimates are not measured engine horsepower or torque.",null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null)
